# Own-wording spells of Valda's Spire of Secrets (2014 rules), part D. Duplicate source names are keyed "Name|<level>".
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Paradox": ["60 ft. Undo one action taken in range within the last round. Its direct effects reverse and its actor takes 10d8 psychic.",
 "60 ft. You twist time into knots and undo one action of your choice taken within range during the last round. Reality recoils from the damage. The direct effects of the action, such as damage from an attack or spell, are undone, but indirect effects, such as creatures choosing to move elsewhere, are not. The creature that took the action takes 10d8 psychic damage as its history is rewritten."],
"Perforating Smite": ["Bonus Action, self, Concentration, 1 minute. Your next firearm shot becomes a 5 ft wide line: Dexterity save for the weapon's damage, half on a save.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. The next time you attack with a firearm before the spell ends, the shot is charged with great power. Instead of an attack roll against one target, it becomes a 5-foot-wide line from you out to the weapon's normal range. Each creature in the line makes a Dexterity save, taking the weapon's normal damage on a failure or half on a success."],
"Petal Storm": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A 15 ft cube of swirling wind heavily obscures its area and deals 3d4 slashing (Strength save) and you can move it 30 ft.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Choose an unoccupied 15-foot cube of air you see in range. A swirling elemental wind fills it for the duration and heavily obscures the area. A creature that enters it for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there makes a Strength save, taking 3d4 slashing damage on a failure. As a Bonus Action you can move the storm up to 30 feet. If the area holds leaf litter, flowers, bushes or trees, the storm sucks up the material and its damage rises by 2d4." + HL + "The damage rises by 3d4 for each slot level above 2."],
"Phantasmal Beauty": ["120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A creature's deepest desire appears only to it: Wisdom save or incapacitated, cannot move, Disadvantage on Perception.",
 "120 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You tap a creature's dreams and create an illusion of its deepest desire, visible only to it. It makes a Wisdom save. On a failure it is incapacitated and cannot move for the duration, and it has Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks. At the end of each of its turns it can save again, ending the spell on itself on a success."],
"Phantom Grapnel": ["Cantrip, 30 ft. A force chain pulls you to a space or Huge creature, or pulls a Large or smaller creature 10 ft toward you (Strength save).",
 "30 ft. You conjure a chain and hook of force and propel it at a creature or unoccupied space you see. If you target a space or a Huge or larger creature, the grapnel pulls you to it in a straight line, and you provoke opportunity attacks as normal. If you target a Large or smaller creature, you pull it up to 10 feet toward you. The creature can make a Strength save to resist."],
"Pharaoh's Curse": ["10 ft, until dispelled. Constitution save or cursed with mummy rot: no healing and hit point maximum drops 3d6 each day.",
 "10 ft, until dispelled. You open your palm and release a puff of dust, the pestilence of mummy rot. A creature in range makes a Constitution save. On a failure it is cursed with mummy rot. It cannot regain hit points, and its hit point maximum drops by 3d6 for each 24 hours that pass. If the maximum reaches 0, it dies and its body turns to dust. The curse lasts until a spell or effect that cures mummy rot removes it. Remove Curse cast with a 5th-level slot or higher also ends it."],
"Pillar Of Salt": ["120 ft. 10 ft radius: Constitution save or 7d6 necrotic (half on a save). A creature dropped to 0 turns to salt.",
 "120 ft. You deliver a mote of divine wrath to a point you see. Each creature you choose in a 10-foot-radius sphere there makes a Constitution save, taking 7d6 necrotic damage on a failure or half on a success. If the damage drops a creature that failed to 0 hit points, it becomes a pillar of salt." + HL + "The damage rises by 7d6 for each slot level above 3."],
"Polybrachia": ["Touch, Concentration, 10 minutes. A willing target gains two extra arms: hold more gear, Advantage on Athletics with them, and a Bonus Action melee attack.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 10 minutes. Two muscular arms of arcane energy appear on a willing creature you touch. They work fully: they can hold weapons and shields (two two-handed or four one-handed weapons), make somatic components and do other tasks, though they grant no extra actions. The target has Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks made with them. If the arms carry weapons, the target can use a Bonus Action to make an extra melee weapon attack with them."],
"Prehensile Hair": ["Self, 1 hour. Long strong hair performs simple tasks within 10 ft and delivers Touch spells at 10 ft.",
 "Self, 1 hour. You grow long, tough hair, even from your eyebrows, that you control at will. It can do simple tasks within 10 feet of you: handle an object, open an unlocked door or container, stow or fetch an item from an open container, or pour out a vial. You can deliver spells with a range of Touch through it, at up to 10 feet. Your hair returns to normal when the spell ends."],
"Protect Threshold": ["Touch, 10 minutes. Ward a doorway: creatures passing take 4d6 psychic (Wisdom save for half).",
 "Touch, 10 minutes. Tracing arcane sigils along its edge, you ward a doorway, window or other portal. For the duration, an invisible eldritch creature stalks it. A creature that tries to pass through makes a Wisdom save, taking 4d6 psychic damage on a failure or half on a success." + HL + "The damage rises by 4d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Protection From Ballistics": ["Touch, Concentration, 1 minute. Firearm attacks against the target have Disadvantage, and it resists firearm damage.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 1 minute. A shimmering shield of energy surrounds a willing creature you touch. For the duration, ranged firearm attacks against it have Disadvantage and it has Resistance to damage from firearms."],
"Psychedelics": ["60 ft, 1 round. Chosen creatures make a Dexterity save or have Disadvantage on attacks until the end of their next turn. Colors change for 1 hour.",
 "60 ft, 1 round. The colors around you swirl in a rainbow and settle far from their usual hues. Each creature you choose in range makes a Dexterity save. On a failure it has Disadvantage on attack rolls until the end of its next turn. The colors of all creatures and objects you choose in range also change at random and stay unnaturally bright for 1 hour."],
"Quickstep": ["Cantrip, Bonus Action, self, 1 round. +10 ft Speed until the start of your next turn.",
 "Self, 1 round. You draw on your inner reserves for a flash of speed. Your base Speed rises by 10 feet until the start of your next turn."],
"Ray of Warping": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Ranged spell attack for 2d8 bludgeoning, halved Speed, and your highest ability drops to its lowest.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A sapphire beam leaps from your fingertips and twists the form of a creature. Make a ranged spell attack against a target you see in range. On a hit it takes 2d8 bludgeoning damage and, for the duration, its Speed is halved and its highest ability score is reduced to equal its lowest (minimum 3). If several scores tie for highest, you choose which drops. It also has Disadvantage on saves with its lowest ability scores. On its turn it can use its action to make a Constitution save, ending the spell on a success." + HL + "With a 4th-level slot or higher the initial damage rises by 1d8 per slot level above 3. With a 7th-level slot or higher the creature's second highest ability score is also reduced to equal its lowest."],
"Recall": ["Bonus Action, self, 1 round. Mark your position, then use your Reaction before your next turn ends to teleport back.",
 "Self, 1 round. Record where you stand when you cast this spell. Until the end of your next turn you can use your Reaction to teleport back to that spot, or to the nearest unoccupied space. If you use it in response to an attack, spell, or other damaging effect, resolve the triggering effect before teleporting."],
"Repulsor Ring": ["5 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. A 5 ft warded circle: only chosen creatures can enter, ranged attacks into it have Disadvantage, and melee attackers are pushed 10 ft.",
 "5 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You outline a 5-foot-diameter circle on the ground, warded against intruders. Only creatures you choose can step inside. Ranged attack rolls against a target in the circle have Disadvantage. If a hostile creature makes a melee attack against a target in the circle, the attacker is pushed back 10 feet right after the attack."],
"Ruby-Eye Curse": ["Touch, Concentration, 10 minutes. Constitution save or the target sees only 5 ft and is blinded beyond.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 10 minutes. A red haze clouds the eyes of a creature that meets your gaze. Choose a creature you see in range. It makes a Constitution save or is cursed for the duration. A cursed target sees normally out to 5 feet but is blinded beyond that. Remove Curse ends it."],
"Rumbling Charge": ["Self. Move 30 ft in a line with no opportunity attacks. Blocking creatures or objects take 2d12 bludgeoning (Strength save for half).",
 "Self. You take on the power of a landslide and at once move 30 feet in a straight line without provoking opportunity attacks. If a creature or object blocks your path, you stop and it makes a Strength save, taking 2d12 bludgeoning damage on a failure or half on a success." + HL + "The damage rises by 2d12 for every two slot levels above 1."],
"Rumor": ["100 ft, 1 minute. Spread a 10 word rumor: nearby intelligent creatures with three or more same-language creatures near them hear it from someone close.",
 "100 ft, 1 minute. You spread a rumor of 10 words or fewer. Any intelligent creature in range that stands near three or more creatures sharing its language believes it hears the rumor repeated by someone nearby. Different creatures hear it from different people, so no origin can be traced. Creatures are rarely openly hostile even at a vicious rumor, but it can shift their disposition for better or worse."],
"Rusting Grasp|2": ["Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Melee spell attack for 2d6 acid and -1 to nonmagical armor AC, or a shield on a miss. Repeat each turn.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Your acid-soaked hand corrodes metal and burns flesh. Make a melee spell attack against a creature in reach. On a hit it takes 2d6 acid damage, and any nonmagical armor it wears takes a permanent, cumulative -1 penalty to the AC it gives. On a miss, a shield it wields takes the same -1 penalty. Armor reduced to AC 10 or a shield reduced to +0 is destroyed. Until the spell ends you can make the attack again as an action on each of your turns." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Rusting Grasp|3": ["Touch. Melee spell attack for 6d4 acid and corrode nonmagical metal armor by -3 AC or destroy a shield, or a 1 ft cube of an object.",
 "Touch. You conjure potent acid at your fingertips that corrodes metal and burns flesh. Make a melee spell attack against a creature or object in reach. On a hit a creature takes 6d4 acid damage, and if it wears nonmagical metal armor or wields a nonmagical metal shield, you can corrode one of them. Corroded armor takes a permanent, cumulative -3 penalty to its AC, and armor reduced to AC 10 is destroyed. A corroded shield is destroyed. Against a nonmagical metal object that is not worn or carried, you corrode and destroy parts of your choice that fit in a 1-foot cube." + HL + "The damage rises by 6d4 for each slot level above 3, and you destroy one extra cubic foot of an object for each slot level above 3."],
"Scrutinize Foe": ["60 ft. Learn two of a creature's AC, current hit points, condition immunities, damage immunities, resistances, vulnerabilities or active spells.",
 "60 ft. You discern fine details about one creature you see in range. Choose two to learn: its AC, current hit points, condition immunities, damage immunities, damage resistances, damage vulnerabilities, or enchantments (which shows spells currently affecting it). The GM must share the information you ask for."],
"Skirmish": ["Touch, Concentration, 10 minutes. A willing target has doubled Speed, ignores nonmagical difficult terrain and provokes no opportunity attacks.",
 "Touch, Concentration, 10 minutes. You boost one willing creature you touch so it moves easily through enemy formations. For the duration its Speed is doubled, it ignores nonmagical difficult terrain, and it provokes no opportunity attacks."],
"Snakestaff": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. A staff becomes a giant constrictor snake friendly to you, obeying verbal commands for free.",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 hour. You cast a staff to the ground and it writhes into a giant constrictor snake under your control, acting on its own initiative. It is friendly to you and your companions and obeys your spoken commands, which cost you no action. Without commands it defends itself and does nothing else. At 0 hit points it dies and returns to a broken staff. The GM has its statistics."],
"Sonic Pulse": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. Constitution save or 1d8 thunder and deafened until your next turn. d10s within 10 ft.",
 "60 ft. You compress a thunderous boom into an invisible ball and send it at a creature you see. It makes a Constitution save or takes 1d8 thunder damage and is deafened until the start of your next turn. If the target is within 10 feet of you, the damage dice are d10s instead.\n\nThe damage rises by one die at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Spark of Life": ["Cantrip, 60 ft. A corpse dead under an hour stands, moves 15 ft and slams a target using your spell attack modifier for size-based bludgeoning.",
 "60 ft. A jolt of necromantic energy makes the dead rise to obey you for a few seconds. Choose the corpse of a Huge or smaller creature that has been dead no more than an hour. It stands, moves up to 15 feet and makes one melee slam against a target you choose in its reach, using your spell attack modifier. A hit deals bludgeoning damage by size: Tiny 1d4, Small 1d6, Medium 1d8, Large 1d10, Huge 1d12. Afterward it collapses. The corpse does not become undead.\n\nAt level 5 the corpse deals two damage dice by size, at level 11 three dice, at level 17 four."],
"Springheel": ["Cantrip, Bonus Action, self, 1 round. Jump 10 ft farther and make running jumps from a standstill.",
 "Self, 1 round. You flood your legs with magic to bound high from a standstill. Your jump distance rises by 10 feet until the start of your next turn, and you can make a running high or long jump without a running start."],
"Stone Bones": ["Bonus Action, self. A creature you see gains Resistance to nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing until the end of its next turn.",
 "Range self, 1 round. You magically reinforce a creature you see in range, giving it Resistance to nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage until the end of its next turn."],
"Swift Flight": ["Touch, Bonus Action. Target gains a 30 ft fly Speed until the end of its next turn.",
 "Touch, 1 round. Streaks of energy trace wings along the back of a creature you touch. Until the end of its next turn it has a flying Speed of 30 feet. It falls if it ends its turn in the air with nothing holding it up."],
"Séance": ["Self, 1 minute, 10 minute cast. With three willing creatures, call a spirit you know to answer three questions.",
 "Self, 1 minute, casting time 10 minutes. You and at least three willing creatures join hands and conjure a spirit to answer questions. Describe or name a creature familiar to you. If its soul is free and willing, it appears as a ghostly specter. The spell fails if that spirit was the target of this spell in the last 10 days. Until it ends you can ask the specter up to three questions. It knows only what it knew in life, including languages. Answers are brief, cryptic or repetitive, and it need not answer truthfully if you are hostile or it sees you as an enemy. There is a 5 percent chance you contact the wrong spirit, which answers falsely or vaguely."],
"Tag": ["Cantrip, touch. Imprint a vivid image with a 3 word message on a surface. It fades after 7 days and nonmagical cleaning cannot remove it.",
 "Touch. You press your hand against a flat surface on an object and imprint an elaborate, vivid image. It can hold a message of up to three words and include art, caricatures or logos in any colors you decide at casting. Nonmagical cleaning supplies cannot remove it, and it fades after seven days."],
"Thunderous Distortion": ["Cantrip, 10 ft cone. Constitution save or 1d6 thunder, heard 100 ft away. Casting again before your next turn ends makes it d8s.",
 "10-foot cone. You produce a distorted wave of noise heard up to 100 feet away. Each creature in the cone makes a Constitution save or takes 1d6 thunder damage. An echo lingers until the end of your next turn. If you cast the spell again before then, the damage dice are d8s.\n\nThe damage rises by 1d6 at level 5, 11 and 17."],
"Time Hop": ["Bonus Action, self. Vanish for 1 to 3 rounds and reappear at the start of your turn, untouchable meanwhile.",
 "Self. You shunt yourself a few seconds into the future. Choose 1, 2 or 3 rounds. You vanish and reappear at the start of your turn after that time, in the nearest unoccupied space to where you vanished. While gone you are outside time: you cannot take actions or reactions, no time passes for you, and nothing can affect you." + HL + "With a 3rd-level slot or higher you can choose a duration of 1 minute. With a 5th-level slot or higher you can choose 1 hour."],
"Time's Arrow": ["Touch, 1 hour. Freeze a missile in place. It fires 120 ft when triggered and attacks with your spell attack bonus.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You enchant a missile of a pound or less (an arrow, bolt or sling bullet) so it freezes in time and space, and you can reposition it as part of casting. It stays until a creature passes within 120 feet in front of it, something touches it, strong wind blows on it, the enchantment is dispelled or the duration ends. Then it shoots off as if fired or thrown with 120 feet of range. If a creature is in the line, the missile makes an attack adding your spell attack bonus, and deals the basic damage of its missile type (use the highest damage dice if it varies by launcher)."],
"Transient Bulwark": ["Self, 8 hours. The next attack against you has a -10 penalty to hit.",
 "Self, 8 hours. The next attack made against you during the duration has a -10 penalty to hit. The material component is a pearl worth 10 gp, which the spell consumes."],
"Tyra's Coerced Karaoke": ["30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Creatures near you make a Wisdom save or sing along and cannot speak normally or use verbal components.",
 "30 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Spectral instruments play around you as you sing a well-known song, and others feel compelled to join. For the duration, when a creature comes within 30 feet of you or starts a turn there, it makes a Wisdom save or sings along. A singing creature matches the pitch and words as best it can, even if it does not speak the language. It cannot speak normally (though it can still communicate telepathically) and cannot use the verbal components of spells. Creatures that cannot be charmed are immune. You can concentrate on this spell and Otto's Irresistible Dance together, and losing concentration on either ends both."],
"Unseen Accountant": ["60 ft, 8 hours. An invisible servant (AC 10, 1 hit point, Int 12) does clerical tasks like pricing, accounts and inventory.",
 "60 ft, 8 hours. You create an invisible, shapeless force that performs intellectual tasks at your command. It appears in an unoccupied space on the ground in range with AC 10, 1 hit point and Intelligence 12, and it cannot attack. At 0 hit points the spell ends. Once on each of your turns as a Bonus Action you can mentally command it to move up to 15 feet and interact with an object. It can do clerk work: assess prices, update accounts, manage inventories, compute interest. It works at a task until done, then waits. It does no physical labor and cannot lift more than 1 pound. If a task would take it more than 300 feet from you, the spell ends."],
"Watery Tentacles": ["Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Three water tentacles grapple and restrain Large or smaller creatures within 30 ft (Strength save), drag 20 ft and lift 100 lb each.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Three tentacles of water appear around your body for the duration. As part of the casting action, and as a Bonus Action on later turns, you can command one tentacle to grapple a Large or smaller creature you see within 30 feet. It makes a Strength save or is grappled and restrained. At the end of each of its turns a restrained target repeats the save, freeing itself on a success. You can grapple as many creatures as you have tentacles. You can use an action or Bonus Action to release a creature or to drag it up to 20 feet in a direction you choose. Tentacles can also manipulate objects as an action or Bonus Action. Each lifts up to 100 pounds, and several can lift one object together. They cannot do fine work, such as opening a chest or uncorking a bottle. Burning objects they grab are put out." + HL + "You gain one extra tentacle for each slot level above 4."],
"Whispering Wind": ["1 mile, 1 round. Whisper a 25 word message on the wind to up to six creatures in the direction you point.",
 "1 mile, 1 round. You point in a direction and whisper a message of 25 words or fewer, naming up to six target creatures. A target in range and in the approximate direction hears the message on the wind, and only they do. They can whisper a reply only you can hear. You need a clear path for air between you and the targets. It can bend around corners and through openings but is blocked by solid objects and magical silence."],
"Wildfire": ["60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. Ten 5 ft cubes of fire that grow by ten each turn deal 8d8 fire (Dexterity save for half).",
 "60 ft, Concentration, 1 minute. You create magical fire filling ten 5-foot cubes on the ground, arranged as you like in range. Each cube must share a face with another. On each of your later turns you can use a Bonus Action to extend the fire by up to ten more cubes, each sharing a face with another cube of fire. The fire damages objects in the area and ignites flammable objects that are not worn or carried. When a creature moves into the fire for the first time or starts its turn there, it makes a Dexterity save, taking 8d8 fire damage on a failure or half on a success."],
"Winter Flower": ["120 ft, 24 hours. A Tiny flower you can command to explode in ice: 30 ft, 10d8 cold (Dexterity save for half). Permanent after 7 days.",
 "120 ft, 24 hours. A Tiny white flower sprouts at a point on the ground you see. It has AC 15, 1 hit point, vulnerability to fire and immunity to cold. During the duration you can use a Bonus Action to command it to burst in a shower of ice. Each creature within 30 feet makes a Dexterity save, taking 10d8 cold damage on a failure or half on a success. The flower withers if it does not explode within 24 hours. Casting the spell again while it lives extends it another 24 hours. Cast on the same flower for seven days, it becomes permanent."],
"Zephyr's Feather": ["Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Three orbiting razor feathers: ranged spell attack for 2d8 slashing now and once per turn as an action.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. You wave your hand and three alabaster feathers, sharpened to a razor edge, orbit you. When you cast it, make a ranged spell attack with a feather against a creature within 120 feet, dealing 2d8 slashing damage on a hit. Until the spell ends, while you have feathers left, you can attack with a feather on each of your turns as an action." + HL + "The damage rises by 2d8 for each slot level above 1, to a maximum of 6d8. You gain two extra feathers with a 3rd-level slot or higher (5 feathers) and two more with a 5th-level slot or higher (7 feathers)."],
}
